.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-template-create - Capture a server as a template


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro template create  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Capture a server as a template

.PP
Billed 0.05 EUR per GB-month of the space the template really uses, hourly from the prepaid balance (through the account's template storage service, opened with the first template). Deleting a template stops its charge. At most 10 templates; visible only in your account. Only the root disk is copied. \fBmode: snapshot\fR (default) keeps the server running (file system frozen briefly via a temporary snapshot); \fBmode: shutdown\fR stops the server, copies it and starts it again. Servers created from the template get a new host name, IP, root password, SSH host keys and machine id (cloud-init); your users, files and settings stay. Linux servers only. Ready in about a minute (\fBstatus\fR creating -> ready).

.PP
API: POST /cloud/servers/{id}/templates (operationId createTemplate, scope cloud_write)


